sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch04-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch04-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch04-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch04-10: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.558"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Failure of later sperm is not itself a tension measurement, but tension, membrane potential and envelope elevation have all been recorded often enough to compile a partial test. The rivals make different predictions, so the inference from polyspermy block to surface tension is decidable where those series exist. They do not yet cover animal eggs at large, and they are not in one archive." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Measure egg cortical tension immediately before and after the first sperm enters, and record whether later sperm are excluded when tension is experimentally held flat. A prompt tension increase that is required for the block would support the claim; exclusion of later sperm by membrane potential or a fertilization envelope, with tension unchanged, would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Tension time series at fertilization are in papers on a few model eggs.", "The electrical fast block and the cortical-granule envelope are confounded with any tension change if they are not measured separately.", "Species differ in which block acts first." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch04-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch04-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.7" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
